WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:05.880
As we all know, Netflix giveth, and Netflix
taketh away and lo and behold, it's taking

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:09.410
away quite a few really great flicks during
March 2020.

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:13.450
It can be difficult to keep track of all the
comings and goings on Netflix, but fortunately

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:16.330
for you, we're on top of it.

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:20.020
Most of Marvel Studios' releases have already
boogied off of Netflix and onto their new

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:24.720
home on rival streamer Disney+, and the stragglers
won't be around for long.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.710
As of now, you can still catch Avengers: Infinity
War, Ant-Man and the Wasp, and Black Panther

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:35.821
on Netflix but if you're keen to relive King
T'Challa's awesome 2018 solo adventure, you'd

00:00:35.821 --> 00:00:37.520
better do it pretty soon.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.110
Time's running out, so don't freeze.

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:43.490
"I never freeze."

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:49.050
Star Chadwick Boseman gives a powerful, regal
performance, his co-stars Danai Gurira and

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:53.219
Letitia Wright deliver star-making turns,
and Michael B. Jordan brings to life one of

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:57.050
the Marvel Cinematic Universe's most complex
villains to date.

00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:01.550
Black Panther is one of Mighty Marvel's greatest
films, and that is really saying something.

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:04.530
Stream it on Netflix until March 3.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:09.690
The franchise may have flagged a bit with
last year's soft reboot Men in Black: International,

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:14.290
but the first three films in the MiB series
the ones which benefited from the sure direction

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:19.240
of Barry Sonnenfeld and the otherworldly comedic
chemistry of stars Tommy Lee Jones and Will

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:22.490
Smith are about as good as sci-fi comedies
get.

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:27.990
The first two of those, 1997's Men in Black
and 2002's Men in Black II, are available

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:30.900
for streaming on Netflix, but not for long.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:35.290
If you haven't caught either of these flicks
for awhile, it will amaze you to be reminded

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:39.140
just how fun and funny they are especially
the first one.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:44.939
Smith's ever-inflating charisma and star power
is on full display, Jones is as cool as ever,

00:01:44.939 --> 00:01:50.530
and supporting players such as Linda Fiorentino,
the late Rip Torn, Lara Flynn Boyle, and Johnny

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:54.880
Knoxville round out the supporting casts of
Men in Black and Men in Black II; watch them

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:57.670
again on Netflix until March 14.

00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:02.680
Coraline is an innovative animated film which
everyone assumes was directed by Tim Burton,

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:07.490
but was actually the work of Henry Selick,
one of Burton's longtime associates and director

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:10.129
of the holiday classic The Nightmare Before
Christmas.

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:15.640
Based on a novel by master of dark fantasy
Neil Gaiman the mind behind the iconic comic

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:20.940
book series The Sandman Coraline goes to some
very unusual places, not the least of which

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:24.050
is the alternate dimension visited by its
child protagonist.

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:25.050
"No way!

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:27.530
You're not sewing buttons in my eyes!"

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:31.190
"Oh, but we need a 'Yes!' if you wanna stay
here."

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:34.050
"So sharp, you won't feel a thi-Ow!"

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:38.940
Basically, it's a stunning visual and narrative
achievement, one which you'll want to catch

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:43.110
again before its time on Netflix is up and
if you've never seen it, you'll probably want

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:44.170
to get on that.

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:47.650
Coraline is available to stream until March
15.

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:53.090
David Fincher's 2007 masterpiece Zodiac is
several cuts above your average true-crime

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:58.340
thriller; meticulously researched, flawlessly
written, and featuring a crackerjack cast

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:03.590
made up largely of, coincidentally, future
MCU alumni, the movie provides an exhaustive

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:08.580
examination of the Zodiac murders, perhaps
the most notorious unsolved serial killings

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:09.909
in American history.

00:03:09.909 --> 00:03:14.879
Like the real-life case, it's agonizingly
suggestive without providing answers; also

00:03:14.879 --> 00:03:19.709
like the case, it can at times slow to a crawl
before catching the viewer totally off-guard

00:03:19.709 --> 00:03:22.460
with shocking, punishing bursts of violence.

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:26.310
David Fincher's direction has never been sharper
or more deliberate.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:29.510
Stream Zodiac on Netflix until March 19.

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:33.020
The films of director Christopher Nolan's
Dark Knight trilogy are some of the finest

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:37.810
examples of the superhero genre, and they
blazed more trails than you might remember.

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:43.230
Before 2005's Batman Begins, the word "reboot"
was used solely to describe the process of

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:49.870
restarting a computer; Nolan's complete revamping
of Batman for the big screen was gritty, grounded,

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:54.200
and inspired, even if its took audiences forever
to get their heads around the fact that it

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:58.780
was not a sequel to the Tim Burton or Joel
Schumacher Batman movies.

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:07.530
"It's not who I am underneath, but what I
do that defines me."

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:08.530
"Bruce?"

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:13.001
The film's legacy would have been impressive
enough on its own, but then came 2008's The

00:04:13.001 --> 00:04:17.940
Dark Knight, which simply shattered everyone's
notions of what a comic book film could be.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:21.380
Sadly, all good things as they say must come
to an end.

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:24.300
Gotham's protector won't be sticking around
for much longer.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:29.650
Batman Begins and The Dark Knight will be
available to stream until March 30.

00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:34.860
Spectacle movies don't get much more spectacular
than Peter Jackson's Lord of the Rings trilogy,

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:39.010
and the second and third films The Two Towers
and The Return of the King are revered by

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:40.580
fans of J.R.R.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.300
Tolkien's classic fantasy novels.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:47.720
Sure, Return of the King ends about six different
times, but fans didn't mind; heck, the movie

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:52.570
was so good that they probably would have
been fine with two or three more fakeout endings.

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:56.840
Mind-blowingly staged and perfectly cast,
the Lord of the Rings flicks set a standard

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:01.250
for big-budget fantasy that no movie without
Harry Potter in the title has even come close

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:02.390
to approaching.

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:04.470
Unfortunately, the end is nigh.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:08.770
You'd best feast your eyes on the final two
films in the greatest fantasy series of all

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:10.530
time before it's too late.

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:14.220
The Lord of the Rings: The Two Towers and
The Lord of the Rings: The Return of the King

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:17.410
will be departing Netflix on March 30.

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:22.200
Its five sequels have provided somewhat diminishing
returns, but it's hard to overstate what a

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:26.710
revelation Paranormal Activity was when it
hit screens in 2007.

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:31.460
Its inspired tweak to the conventions of the
found-footage genre: all of the action takes

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:35.860
place on cameras which a young couple set
up throughout their home in an attempt to

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:40.690
record, well, the paranormal activity plaguing
the joint, allowed it to be made on a shoestring

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:41.690
budget.

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:49.120
This a) in no way kept it from being the scariest
film of its year, and b) made its $193 million

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:53.100
worldwide box office total even more impressive
than if the film hadn't been made for the

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:55.260
cost of a pretty nice used car.

00:05:55.260 --> 00:06:02.980
"You know what, there's footsteps in but there's
no footsteps out."

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:04.389
"Oh, God."

00:06:04.389 --> 00:06:09.140
Director Oren Peli masterfully ratchets up
the tension during the film's scant 85-minute

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:14.800
run time, and then-unknown stars Katie Featherston
and Micah Sloat turn in realistic performances

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:17.940
that make the frequent scares land that much
harder.

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:22.470
With an excruciating third act and a final
shot guaranteed to separate you from your

00:06:22.470 --> 00:06:27.551
skin, Paranormal Activity is one of the very
best found-footage flicks ever made; stream

00:06:27.551 --> 00:06:30.220
it on Netflix until March 30.

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:34.231
As a director, Quentin Tarantino is every
bit as skilled as he is wildly unrestrained,

00:06:34.231 --> 00:06:37.350
and we love him for both of those qualities.

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:42.699
Kill Bill Vol. 1 and Kill Bill Vol. 2 are
very much two halves of one big movie, and

00:06:42.699 --> 00:06:46.520
it is part kung-fu flick, part revenge movie,
and all Tarantino.

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:53.389
Uma Thurman stars as Beatrix Kiddo AKA "The
Bride" a master assassin and once a key member

00:06:53.389 --> 00:06:56.020
of the feared Deadly Viper Assassination Squad.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:07:00.759
She is brutalized and left for dead on her
wedding day by her former cohorts, including

00:07:00.759 --> 00:07:05.580
their leader, Bill, who responds to her plea
to spare her life and the life of their unborn

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:07.710
child by shooting her in the head.

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:12.090
Over the course of the two movies, she exacts
her revenge on the Squad's members without

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:17.680
mercy, eventually fulfilling the flicks' titles
by way of the Five Point Palm Exploding Heart

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:18.680
Technique.

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:20.100
"You're a terrific person.

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:22.380
You're my favorite person.

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:28.590
But every once in a while, you can be a real
c----."

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:34.199
The Kill Bill flicks are pure, distilled Tarantino
which is to say that they are uber-cinematic,

00:07:34.199 --> 00:07:36.940
super-stylized, unbelievably violent fun.

00:07:36.940 --> 00:07:41.060
They are two of the straight-up craziest movies
you will ever see, and you've only got so

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:46.259
much time left to see them on Netflix; Kill
Bill Vol. 1 and Kill Bill Vol. 2 will be leaving

00:07:46.259 --> 00:07:48.129
the streamer on March 30.

